LAWS REQUIRED: associative, identity, inverses
   integers mod 7 under + (inverse is 7 − n)
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is 0
     inverses:    True
     commutative: True
   nonzero fractions (sample) under ×
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is 1
     inverses:    True
     commutative: True
   the 6 permutations of 3 objects under composition
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is (0, 1, 2)
     inverses:    True
     commutative: False   fails at (0, 2, 1), (1, 0, 2)
   ℕ 0..6 under + (the non-example)
     associative: True
     identity:    True   it is 0
     inverses:    False   none for 1, 2, 3
     commutative: True
   in a group every row of the table is a rearrangement of the set (a Latin square):
     (0, 1, 2) ∘ _ : True
     (0, 2, 1) ∘ _ : True
     (1, 0, 2) ∘ _ : True
